# Words that must not appear in the folder. Every entry here is made up.
#
# Copy this file to .jidoka-scrub-words in the folder that you scrub, or pass
# its path as the second argument of checks/scrub.sh. Put your own words in it.
# Keep your copy out of version control: it names what it hides.
#
# One word or pattern on each line. Case does not matter.
# A pattern is an extended regular expression.
# A line that starts with # is a comment. To search for a # sign, write [#].

# A product name and its code name.
zorblat
project[ -]?quuxmill

# A short name that is also the start of a common word: say what may not follow it.
zorb([^a-z]|$)

# A company.
fernwick (and|&) dobbs

# A person.
pat[ .]?exampleson

# An account or a team identifier.
ZB-[0-9]{6}
app\.zorblat\.[a-z]+

# A host that is not written as a link.
zorblat-api\.[a-z]{2,}

# A ticket or pull request number of another project.
[#][0-9]{2,5}

# A home folder of a machine.
/(Users|home)/[a-z0-9._-]+/
